cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Paper2Bench — evidence-first reproduction workspace for ML papers
message: >-
  If you use Paper2Bench in your research workflow, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - name: Paper2Bench Contributors
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-26"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/paper2bench/paper2bench"
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - machine learning
  - evidence
  - experiment scaffolds
  - research engineering
abstract: >-
  Paper2Bench turns an ML paper into an evidence-backed, inspectable experiment:
  claim-level extraction with source spans, honest unknown/conflict states,
  deterministic PyTorch/HuggingFace scaffolds, run provenance, and
  reported-vs-measured comparison under explicit protocol criteria.
